            "(`seon.test-support/evaluate` {`:seon.cluster.eval/source` \"#:seon.repl{:value 1}\" ...}) whose only form the batch refuses (:seon.batch/refused :fabricated-response) answers nil: the last entry has no `:seon.batch/evaluation`, so the function's own :map output contract refuses with a contract error instead of the refusal (seen by the reader-prose lane's forgive_test on a check JVM, 2026-10-07). Correct: the refused entry's error reaches the caller as data, as evaluate-row builds an unrun evaluation for it in the turn. Read `seon.turn/evaluate-row`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-test-member-connection-is-not-the-cluster-head"
             :intent "A test member's connection is its own branch, not the cluster head, so a test of a function that compares a branch with its cluster head (RF-1, 24e8cc2df: `my.program/write-branch!`, `my.program/diff`) must build its own cluster-<name> branch by hand. Correct: one test-support helper gives a member a cluster head and a branch off it, and the clojure-testing skill names it. Proof: a seon.test-support-test deftest (to be written) asserting the helper's branch compares against the head it made. Read `docs/seon/schedule/cards/RF-1.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "file-backed-branch-without-republication"
             :intent "`seon.test-support/with-published-file-database` acquires a Datahike branch of the executing published source, carrying its projection and writing to a private Konserve file frontend. It must preserve real blob staging and independent fixture writes without calling `seon.test-support/populate-published-root!` or `seon.cluster/refresh-source!`. The tagged `seon.test-support-test/a-file-backed-fixture-costs-a-branch` measures complete acquisition, body and release with `seon.profile/measure`, including the remaining `datahike.store/ready-store` synchronization. The owner accepted :tiered with the range-enabled Konserve fork and bounds derived from measured acquisition; removing the file overlay's asynchronous empty-file read is a separate task. Evidence and parent/change costs live in fixture-hour.md. Read `seon.blob/stage-binary!`, `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/fixture-hour.md`, `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/round-waste.md` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/round-waste/evidence.edn`."}
